AHS-018 — Data Architecture

Document ID: AHS-018
Title: Data Architecture
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

Architectural Views: Information, Logical, Implementation

1. Purpose

This specification defines the canonical Data Architecture of the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF).

The Data Architecture establishes the normative organization, lifecycle, governance, relationships, and semantics of engineering data independent of storage technologies, databases, or implementation platforms.

2. Scope

This specification defines:

Data principles
Canonical data model
Data categories
Data ownership
Data relationships
Data lifecycle
Data governance
Version management

This specification does not define databases, persistence technologies, storage engines, or serialization formats.

3. Canonical Definition

Engineering Data is the canonical representation of engineering reality, cognition, decisions, governance, and operational information within the Atlas architecture.

Engineering data SHALL preserve meaning independently of its physical representation.

4. Data Objectives

Atlas data SHALL:

Preserve engineering semantics.
Preserve provenance.
Preserve traceability.
Support explainability.
Be versioned.
Be governed.
Be reusable.
Be technology independent.
5. Data Principles

Every Atlas data element SHALL satisfy the following principles.

Semantic Integrity

Meaning SHALL remain unchanged regardless of storage.

Single Source of Truth

Each canonical entity SHALL have one authoritative owner.

Immutability Where Appropriate

Historical records SHALL remain immutable.

Version Awareness

Every governed data object SHALL support versioning.

Traceability

Relationships SHALL be explicitly represented.

Extensibility

The model SHALL allow future engineering domains without structural redesign.

