      ▼
Decision Record

Supporting relationships include:

references
derives from
validates
supersedes
approves
depends on
influences
generated by

Relationships SHALL be explicitly represented.

9. Data Lifecycle
Created
    │
Validated
    │
Active
    │
Referenced
    │
Versioned
    │
Archived
    │
Retired

Lifecycle transitions SHALL preserve historical integrity.

10. Version Management

Atlas SHALL support:

Major versions
Minor versions
Patch versions

Version history SHALL be immutable.

Superseded versions SHALL remain traceable.

11. Data Ownership

Each canonical entity SHALL define:

Data Owner
Steward
Producer
Consumers
Approval Authority

Ownership responsibilities SHALL be documented.

12. Data Governance

Governed entities SHALL define:

Retention policy
Validation policy
Security classification
Privacy requirements
Audit requirements
Archival policy

Governance SHALL remain independent of implementation.

13. Data Quality

Atlas data SHALL be evaluated for:

Accuracy
Completeness
Consistency
Validity
Timeliness
Uniqueness
Traceability
Explainability

Quality assessments SHALL themselves be traceable.

14. Conformance

An implementation conforms if it:

Uses canonical data entities.
Preserves semantic integrity.
Implements version management.
Maintains explicit relationships.
Enforces governance policies.
15. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY introduce:

Domain-specific entity profiles.
Ontology mappings.
Knowledge graph representations.
Federated engineering data spaces.
Semantic interoperability standards.

Extensions SHALL remain compatible with the canonical data model.